    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Show, using substitution, that $H(-15,8)$ lies on the circle centred at the origin with radius 17.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-15)^2+8^2=225+64=289=17^2$, so $H$ lies on the circle.",
      "worked": "The circle has equation $x^2+y^2=289$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(-15)^2+8^2&=225+64\\\\(-15)^2+8^2&=289\\end{align*}$$\nThe coordinates satisfy the equation, so $H$ lies on the circle.",
